## Case study: bkhack shell

*Companion of `ttb-hcmut/bkhack/src_devbook/streaming.pdf`*

This will involve:
- **The normal parser.** Evaluates shell expression as an emulation of shell-kernel, but is only used to navigate around the website.\
  $ \text{string} : \text{string} \rightarrow \text{result} (\text{program}, \text{string}) $
- **The pasteller.** Provides real-time syntax highlighting for the command bar.\
  $ \text{string} : \text{string} \rightarrow \text{result} (\text{element}, \text{string}) $

